Module 3: Preamplifier and Differential Driver

Purpose:
- Adjust signal amplitude to ADC full scale; provide single-ended to differential conversion and low output impedance to drive ADC input.

Schematic description:
- Input NET RF_ATT_OUT -> AC coupling cap (if required) -> matched input network -> Driver IC input
- Driver: AD8138 configured as differential driver. Gain set by Rg per datasheet: G = 1 + (49.9k / Rg) when configured appropriately (consult datasheet). For unity gain use recommended resistor values.
- Output: ADC_IN_P and ADC_IN_N differential pair (100Ω differential impedance)

Components (suggested):
- Differential driver: AD8138 (or THS4509 for higher speed)
- Input matching: 50Ω series resistor or LC matching network as required
- DC bias: Vcm rail from REF/2 via resistor divider and buffer, or follow ADC recommended VCM

Layout notes:
- Short matched differential traces to ADC; place bypass caps close to device pins.
- Minimize series inductance; keep ground plane continuous.

Verification:
- Inject known input sine; measure differential output amplitude and linearity; ensure driver can swing to ADC input range without clipping.
